  "notes": {
    "risersFallers": "Utah and UCLA climb on pure résumé (undefeated + quality wins) relative to pure predictive models that underrate their efficiency. Wake Forest and Texas Tech rise on recent blowouts. Kentucky (loss to Florida) and LSU (loss to Texas) drop hard. Ohio State's predictive strength is real but the 7-3 record correctly tanks the hybrid.",
    "apVsGrok": "Human polls/CFP lean Utah ~2 and UCLA ~4 (record bias). Grok slots Utah 3 and UCLA 8 — rewarding the undefeateds but not ignoring SP+/FPI gaps. BYU and Texas Tech sit higher in Grok than some brand-heavy polls because of efficiency + wins, not name. No brand inflation.",
    "nextWeek": "Utah at TCU, Georgia at South Carolina, UCLA's Big Ten test, Wake Forest road, and Texas Tech/BYU Big 12 games can flip seeds. A Utah loss drops the undefeated boost; a Georgia slip opens the #1. Big 12 chaos especially rearranges the middle.",
    "cfpOutlook": "Projected field (byes to top 4): 1 Georgia (SEC champ path), 2 Utah (Big 12), 3 Notre Dame (independent), 4 Miami (ACC), then Alabama, Indiana, Texas, UCLA, Tennessee, Wake Forest, Texas Tech, BYU. Conference champions likely: Big Ten — UCLA or Indiana; SEC — Georgia or Alabama; Big 12 — Utah or Texas Tech; ACC — Miami or Wake Forest; Independent — Notre Dame locked in; G5 — Boise State or New Mexico for the auto-bid. First-round: higher seeds host. Top 4 byes set up Georgia/Utah/ND/Miami as favorites for deep runs."
  },
